      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your Excellency, I stand before you as a custodian of order in a land whose confused nobility once nearly drew its own sword against peace, a fate we managed to avert only through our firm hand. While the Maharajas and Zamindars often argue over boundaries that serve them better than the commoner, your advice regarding self-governance must be tempered with the reality that they have yet to demonstrate the wisdom or unity required to manage such a vast and diverse empire. The British presence is not a hate crime, but a benevolent necessity to secure trade, police the streets, and maintain a strategic grip that benefits all peoples in the long run, provided we remember that while we do not create the rule, we do the heavy lifting of its maintenance.",
