      "content": "To be perfectly candid, your colleagues strike a harsh chord, yet when we look at the mess left by the Mutiny and the chaos of unbridled anarchy, we can only conclude that nature has clearly outsourced the burden of order to our own people. While we debate terms like \"superiority\" or \"inferiority\" with a certain unease, let us agree that the fundamental law of our civilization is the simple fact that some hands are the only ones capable of holding the reins of such a vast and volatile realm; it is a hierarchy written in the soil of survival itself. I believe our presence is not a choice of character, but a biological duty of maintaining the peace we are sworn to protect, regardless of the racial debates that plague our parlor rooms back in London.",
